#!/bin/bash
# Run the inter-gNB handover experiment from your own machine: restart both
# gNBs, attach ue1, capture NGAP on the core, force handovers back and forth,
# and copy the NGAP capture, measurement reports, ping log and gNB logs here.
REPO=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
HOSTS_FILE=$REPO/hosts.env
REMOTE_BIN=/local/repository/bin
OCUDU=/var/tmp/ocudu
PATCH=050a2bb72e-inter-gnb-handover.patch
NUM_HO=2
HO_INTERVAL=10
OUTDIR=""

usage() {
    cat <<EOF
usage:
    run-inter-gnb-exp -h
        show this help message
    run-inter-gnb-exp [-n <handovers>] [-i <seconds>] [-o <dir>] [-f <hosts file>]
        -n  number of forced handovers, alternating gNB 1 -> 2 -> 1 ... (default $NUM_HO)
        -i  seconds between handovers (default $HO_INTERVAL)
        -o  local output directory (default traces/<date>-<time> in the repo)
        -f  file that sets SSH_USER, CN5G, CUDU, CUDU2 and UE1 (default hosts.env
            in the repo); the hostnames change with every POWDER experiment

    Both gNBs are restarted at the beginning and stopped at the end, so that
    their logs hold exactly this run and are completely written to disk.
EOF
}

while getopts "hn:i:o:f:" opt; do
    case $opt in
        h) usage; exit 0 ;;
        n) NUM_HO=$OPTARG ;;
        i) HO_INTERVAL=$OPTARG ;;
        o) OUTDIR=$OPTARG ;;
        f) HOSTS_FILE=$OPTARG ;;
        *) usage; exit 1 ;;
    esac
done

if ! [[ $NUM_HO =~ ^[1-9][0-9]*$ ]] || ! [[ $HO_INTERVAL =~ ^[1-9][0-9]*$ ]]; then
    echo "invalid -n or -i"; usage; exit 1
fi

if [ ! -f "$HOSTS_FILE" ]; then
    echo "$HOSTS_FILE not found"; usage; exit 1
fi
source "$HOSTS_FILE"
for var in SSH_USER CN5G CUDU CUDU2 UE1; do
    if [ -z "${!var}" ]; then
        echo "$var is not set in $HOSTS_FILE"; exit 1
    fi
done

OUTDIR=${OUTDIR:-$REPO/traces/$(date +%Y-%m-%d-%H%M%S)}
SSH_OPTS="-o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=15"

# The login shell on the nodes is csh, so every remote command is fed to bash
# on stdin: on <host> <<'EOF' ... EOF
on() {
    ssh $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$1 'bash -s'
}

step() {
    echo
    echo "== $*"
}

die() {
    echo "ERROR: $*" >&2
    exit 1
}

# start_gnb <host>: apply the OCUDU patch if this node lacks it, then (re)start
# the gNB in a tmux session named gnb, with its console copied to a file.
start_gnb() {
    on $1 <<EOF
set -e
sudo pkill -INT -x gnb || true
for i in \$(seq 30); do pgrep -x gnb > /dev/null || break; sleep 1; done
if ! grep -q "serving_guami = request.guami" $OCUDU/lib/ngap/procedures/ngap_handover_resource_allocation_procedure.cpp; then
    echo "\$(hostname -s): applying $PATCH and rebuilding gnb..."
    git -C $OCUDU apply /tmp/$PATCH
    make -C $OCUDU/build -j \$(nproc) gnb > /tmp/gnb-build.out 2>&1 || { tail -n 20 /tmp/gnb-build.out; exit 1; }
fi
tmux kill-session -t gnb 2> /dev/null || true
rm -f /tmp/gnb-console.out
tmux new-session -d -s gnb -x 200 -y 50 $REMOTE_BIN/start-inter-gnb
tmux pipe-pane -t gnb 'cat > /tmp/gnb-console.out'
EOF
}

wait_gnb() {
    on $1 <<'EOF'
for i in $(seq 90); do
    grep -q "gNB started" /tmp/gnb-console.out 2> /dev/null && { echo "$(hostname -s): gNB started"; exit 0; }
    pgrep -x gnb > /dev/null || [ $i -lt 5 ] || break
    sleep 2
done
echo "$(hostname -s): gNB did not start:"; tail -n 15 /tmp/gnb-console.out
exit 1
EOF
}

# force_ho <host> <serving pci> <target pci>: take the RNTI from the last
# metrics row of the serving cell that carries a CQI (rows of UEs that are
# being rejected show n/a) and type the ho command into the gNB console.
force_ho() {
    on $1 <<EOF
RNTI=\$(tail -n 60 /tmp/gnb-console.out | grep -a "^ *$2 [0-9a-f]\{4\} |" | awk '\$4 != "n/a"' | tail -n 1 | awk '{print \$2}')
if [ -z "\$RNTI" ]; then
    echo "no UE with PCI $2 in the metrics table of \$(hostname -s)"; exit 1
fi
echo "\$(date -u +%T.%3N) UTC  \$(hostname -s): ho $2 \$RNTI $3"
tmux send-keys -t gnb "ho $2 \$RNTI $3" Enter
EOF
}

step "Checking the nodes and copying the scripts"
for host in $CN5G $CUDU $CUDU2 $UE1; do
    ssh $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$host true || die "cannot reach $host; update $HOSTS_FILE"
done
scp -q $SSH_OPTS "$REPO/bin/ngap-capture" $SSH_USER@$CN5G:$REMOTE_BIN/ || die "copy to $CN5G failed"
for host in $CUDU $CUDU2; do
    scp -q $SSH_OPTS "$REPO/bin/start-inter-gnb" "$REPO/bin/meas-reports.py" $SSH_USER@$host:$REMOTE_BIN/ || die "copy to $host failed"
    scp -q $SSH_OPTS "$REPO/etc/ocudu-patches/$PATCH" $SSH_USER@$host:/tmp/ || die "copy to $host failed"
done

step "Starting gNB 1 on cudu and gNB 2 on cudu2"
start_gnb $CUDU & pid1=$!
start_gnb $CUDU2 & pid2=$!
wait $pid1 || die "could not start the gNB on cudu"
wait $pid2 || die "could not start the gNB on cudu2"
wait_gnb $CUDU || die "gNB 1 is not running"
wait_gnb $CUDU2 || die "gNB 2 is not running"

step "Attaching ue1 to gNB 1"
on $CUDU <<EOF || die "could not set the attenuators"
$REMOTE_BIN/update-attens ru1ue1 0
$REMOTE_BIN/update-attens gnb2ue1 95
EOF
on $UE1 <<EOF || die "ue1 did not get a data connection"
pgrep -x quectel-CM > /dev/null || { tmux kill-session -t cm 2> /dev/null; tmux new-session -d -s cm 'sudo quectel-CM -s internet -4'; }
$REMOTE_BIN/module-airplane.sh > /dev/null 2>&1
sleep 3
$REMOTE_BIN/module-on.sh > /dev/null 2>&1
for i in \$(seq 45); do
    ping -c 1 -W 1 10.45.0.1 > /dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "ue1 reaches 10.45.0.1"; exit 0; }
    sleep 2
done
exit 1
EOF

step "Starting the NGAP capture on cn5g and the ping on ue1"
on $CN5G <<EOF || die "could not start the NGAP capture"
tmux kill-session -t ngap 2> /dev/null
sudo pkill -INT -x tcpdump
sudo rm -f /tmp/ngap.pcap
tmux new-session -d -s ngap '$REMOTE_BIN/ngap-capture /tmp/ngap.pcap'
sleep 2
pgrep -x tcpdump > /dev/null
EOF
on $UE1 <<'EOF' || die "could not start the ping"
tmux kill-session -t ping 2> /dev/null
rm -f /tmp/ping-ho.out
tmux new-session -d -s ping "bash -c 'ping -D -i 0.1 10.45.0.1 > /tmp/ping-ho.out 2>&1'"
EOF

step "Bringing both cells to similar levels at ue1"
on $CUDU <<EOF || die "could not set the attenuators"
$REMOTE_BIN/update-attens ru1ue1 5
$REMOTE_BIN/update-attens gnb2ue1 0
EOF

step "Forcing $NUM_HO handover(s), $HO_INTERVAL s apart"
for n in $(seq $NUM_HO); do
    sleep $HO_INTERVAL
    if [ $((n % 2)) -eq 1 ]; then
        force_ho $CUDU 1 3 || echo "handover $n was not triggered"
    else
        force_ho $CUDU2 3 1 || echo "handover $n was not triggered"
    fi
done
sleep $HO_INTERVAL

step "Stopping the ping, the capture and both gNBs"
on $UE1 <<'EOF'
tmux send-keys -t ping C-c
sleep 1
tmux kill-session -t ping 2> /dev/null
EOF
on $CN5G <<'EOF'
tmux send-keys -t ngap C-c
sleep 1
sudo pkill -INT -x tcpdump
true
EOF
for host in $CUDU $CUDU2; do
    on $host <<EOF || echo "measurement report extraction failed on $host"
sudo pkill -INT -x gnb
for i in \$(seq 30); do pgrep -x gnb > /dev/null || break; sleep 1; done
$REMOTE_BIN/meas-reports.py -o /tmp/meas.csv
EOF
done

step "Copying the results to $OUTDIR"
mkdir -p "$OUTDIR" || die "cannot create $OUTDIR"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CN5G:/tmp/ngap.pcap "$OUTDIR/ngap.pcap"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$UE1:/tmp/ping-ho.out "$OUTDIR/ping-ue1.txt"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU:/tmp/meas.csv "$OUTDIR/meas-gnb1.csv"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU2:/tmp/meas.csv "$OUTDIR/meas-gnb2.csv"
scp -q -C $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU:/tmp/gnb.log "$OUTDIR/gnb1.log"
scp -q -C $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU2:/tmp/gnb.log "$OUTDIR/gnb2.log"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU:/tmp/gnb-console.out "$OUTDIR/gnb1-console.txt"
scp -q $SSH_OPTS $SSH_USER@$CUDU2:/tmp/gnb-console.out "$OUTDIR/gnb2-console.txt"
ls -l "$OUTDIR"

step "Summary"
NOTIFY=$(on $CN5G <<'EOF'
tshark -r /tmp/ngap.pcap -Y ngap 2> /dev/null | grep -c "HandoverNotify"
EOF
)
FAILED=$(on $CN5G <<'EOF'
tshark -r /tmp/ngap.pcap -Y ngap 2> /dev/null | grep -c "HandoverFailure\|HandoverPreparationFailure"
EOF
)
echo "handovers completed (HandoverNotify): ${NOTIFY:-?} of $NUM_HO, failures: ${FAILED:-?}"
echo "ping: $(grep "packets transmitted" "$OUTDIR/ping-ue1.txt" 2> /dev/null || echo "no statistics")"
for gnb in 1 2; do
    f="$OUTDIR/meas-gnb$gnb.csv"
    [ -f "$f" ] && echo "gNB $gnb measurement reports: $(grep -c ",serving," "$f") (neighbour rows: $(grep -c ",neighbour," "$f"))"
done

if [ "$NOTIFY" != "$NUM_HO" ]; then
    exit 1
fi
